# {{projectName}}

This project was generated with `dorm_example` using the **{{engine}}** engine.

The application uses one store domain throughout the showcase: users,
categories, products, carts, cart items, reviews, and wishlist items. The
annotated source is in `lib/models.dart`. The `*.dorm.dart` and `*.g.dart`
files are generated and should not be edited manually.

## Run the project

{{#docker}}
Start the local infrastructure first. The Compose file starts services only;
the generated application still runs on the host.

```shell
docker compose up -d
```
{{#firebaseEmulator}}
This profile uses a local Firebase Emulator Suite container with the fictional
project ID `dorm-example`. No Firebase project or credentials are required.
The Realtime Database emulator is available on port `9000`, the Firestore
emulator on port `8080`, and Emulator UI on <http://localhost:4000>.
{{/firebaseEmulator}}
{{#httpServer}}
This profile starts a small in-memory Dart REST server from `./server`. It is
the backend for this generated showcase, not an external production API. Its
data is lost when the container is restarted.
{{/httpServer}}

{{#requiresEnvironment}}
Use `.env.example` as a list of required variables. The generated Dart
application reads the process environment; it does not load `.env` itself.
Export the variables in your shell or configure them in your IDE before
running the application.
{{/requiresEnvironment}}
{{/docker}}

{{#isFlutter}}
Install dependencies, generate the model API, and start the Web application:

```shell
flutter pub get
dart run build_runner build
flutter run -d chrome{{#httpServer}} --dart-define=HTTP_BASE_URI=http://localhost:8080/api/{{/httpServer}}
```

Flutter profiles require Flutter **3.47.1 or newer** because of the
`build_runner` and analyzer dependency constraints.
{{/isFlutter}}
{{^isFlutter}}
Install dependencies, generate the model API, and run the Dart showcase:

```shell
dart pub get
dart run build_runner build
dart analyze
dart run
```
{{/isFlutter}}

## What to inspect

- `lib/models.dart` contains the source annotations.
- `lib/models.dorm.dart` contains the generated repositories and entities.
- `lib/models.g.dart` contains serialization and copy-with support.
{{#jsonFeatures}}
- The JSON-oriented models demonstrate nested data, polymorphic data, and a
  materialized derived value.
{{/jsonFeatures}}
{{^jsonFeatures}}
- The model set intentionally stays relational and uses scalar fields and
  foreign keys instead of JSON-oriented model annotations.
{{/jsonFeatures}}

